# NestJS API (`apps/api`)

Package: `@pcms/api`. Entry: `src/main.ts`. Root module: `src/app.module.ts`.

## Module layout

Each feature under `src/modules/<name>/`:
- `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`
- `dto/` for request/response shapes
- `*.spec.ts` beside each testable unit

Shared code lives in `src/common/` (guards, filters, interceptors, decorators, utils).

## Conventions

- Global prefix: `/api` (set in `main.ts`)
- Config via `ConfigService`: `config.get('database.host')` — namespaces in `src/config/configuration.ts`
- Validation: `class-validator` DTOs + global `ValidationPipe`
- Auth: JWT access token in body; refresh in HttpOnly SameSite=Strict cookie
- RBAC: `@Roles()` + `RolesGuard`; public routes via `@Public()`
- Rate limiting: `@nestjs/throttler` on sensitive auth routes
- Content: Markdown via `marked`, sanitize with DOMPurify (`content.util.ts`)
- Media: Sharp → WebP, local disk under `MEDIA_LOCAL_PATH`

## Database

- Entities: `src/database/entities/`
- Migrations: `src/database/migrations/` — use TypeORM CLI scripts in `package.json`
- Do **not** rely on `synchronize: true` in production paths; use migrations

## Observability

- Logging: Pino via `nestjs-pino`
- Metrics: Prometheus at `/metrics` (not under `/api`)
- Tracing: OpenTelemetry — loaded via `tracing.ts` before `main.ts`
- Health: `@nestjs/terminus` — liveness vs readiness in health module

## Adding endpoints

```typescript
// ✅ Match existing patterns
@Controller('posts')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
export class PostsController {
  @Get('admin')
  @Roles(UserRole.ADMIN, UserRole.EDITOR)
  findAllAdmin() { ... }
}
```

- Permission-check every new route
- Return data through existing interceptors/filters
- Add `*.spec.ts` with mocked repositories/queues — **100% coverage** on included paths

## Testing (Jest)

- Colocate: `foo.service.spec.ts` next to `foo.service.ts`
- Setup: `jest.setup.ts` (reflect-metadata, DOMPurify mock)
- Excluded from coverage: `main.ts`, `*.module.ts`, DTOs, entities, enums, migrations
- Run: `npm run test:cov -w @pcms/api`

## Anti-patterns

- New global providers without wiring in `AppModule`
- Raw SQL when TypeORM repository suffices
- Skipping validation DTOs on POST/PATCH bodies
- Returning unsanitized HTML from user Markdown
- Integration tests in `test/` folder (empty — use unit mocks unless harness is added)
